<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Znojmo</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Znaim</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Znojmo is a town in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czech-republic">Czech Republic</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thaya">Thaya</a> river near the Austrian border. From about 1092 it was the seat of a Přemyslid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appanage">appanage</a> duchy, and the rotunda in its castle preserves 12th-century wall paintings showing rulers of the dynasty. The town became a royal town in the 13th century and is known for its wine.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/znojmo.jpg" alt="Znojmo" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: RomanM82 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Znojmo_-_panorama_od_jihu_obr1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
